# The build context of every KiCI image is the repository root
# (`docker build -f packages/<name>/Dockerfile .`). podman reads an ignore
# file only at the root of the build context, so this file is the one that
# both podman and Docker apply to every COPY. Each image installs its
# dependencies and compiles inside the build. The host's dependency trees,
# build output, local environment files and keys stay out of the context.
.git
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/dist.tmp
**/dist.tmp-*
**/.turbo
**/coverage
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/sbom.spdx.json
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
**/*.pem
**/*.key
